WEBVTT

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.200
I think the biggest thing is just recognizing that we're going to have AI

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.760
forever.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.200
Like there's no getting away from any of that.

00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:14.253
If you don't know how to use it, you're going to fall behind.

00:00:14.193 --> 00:00:19.013
That being said, if that's all you use, you're useless because anyone can

00:00:18.713 --> 00:00:19.633
use AI.

00:00:19.906 --> 00:00:27.246
so if I had an e-bike I know myself well enough that I would probably start

00:00:26.946 --> 00:00:31.186
relying on the e-bike intensively rather than getting a workout that I need

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:35.746
every day So it's so much easier to be complacent when the tool is there.

00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:40.066
Whereas like some people will use e-bikes for mountain biking and they'll

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:42.500
still get really good workouts out of it.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.990
It's not like we can choose to not buy the e-bike.

00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:50.987
Oh, sorry — I bought it yeah I bought it for almost like I literally bought

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:51.833
it for everybody

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.920
I think you know even though it's fictional I think prime examples like

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.660
Tony Stark who you know he knows all the math he knows everything that he

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.486
needs to do where Jarvis is a support to Tony Stark and not doing Tony Stark's

00:01:05.186 --> 00:01:05.833
work

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.960
We about to get YouTube famous.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.140
So, pick up a thousand likes on this.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.033
We're changing our career.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.340
Or maybe I misheard Audrey but I think I heard her say reel — so like you

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.933
know we can make like a reel of us like being this is good this is bad

00:01:21.273 --> 00:01:22.833
We'll probably call it good there.

00:01:23.313 --> 00:01:24.733
Thanks, Audrey, Carl, everybody.
